---
layout: layouts/diffuse.vto
base: ../../
title: Guide | Facets | Diffuse

styles:
  - styles/base.css
  - styles/diffuse/page.css
  - vendor/@phosphor-icons/bold/style.css
  - vendor/@phosphor-icons/fill/style.css
---

{{ await comp.facets.header() }}

<main>
  {{ await comp.facets.nav({ url }) }}

  <section>
    <h1 hidden>Guide</h1>
    <p>
      To use these facets, simply open whichever ones provide the functionality that you're looking for at a given moment. You can browse existing ones here and create one below.
    </p>
    <p>
      For example, say you want to play music; two options would be: (1) <a href="{{ ('themes/webamp/browser/facet/index.html') |> facetLoaderURL }}">browse</a> for a specific song and add it to the queue, or (2) <a href="{{ ('facets/tools/auto-queue/index.html') |> facetLoaderURL }}">automatically</a> add a bunch of shuffled songs to the queue. Next, you need a way to play the items you added to the queue. That's where a <a href="{{ ('themes/blur/artwork-controller/facet/index.html') |> facetLoaderURL }}">controller</a> could be used.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em>You might ask, why can't I do all of this in just one window? That's what <a href="themes/">themes</a> are for, if you need something more streamlined. If you however want a customised experience, or prefer certain interfaces for certain things, that's what facets are for.</em>
    </p>
    <p>
      <small><i class="ph-fill ph-info"></i> Every facet has access to your audio collection and your user data, along with any other shared state.</small>
    </p>
  </section>
</main>
